paper/main.tex:192:The controls support this explanation without proving it for other tasks. Literal wording improved matched accuracy by \literalControlChange{} points, with \literalControlWins{} wins and no losses. Across all outputs, distractor capture was \distractorCaptureRate{}\%, exact-output compliance was \exactOutputComplianceRate{}\%, and invalid output was \invalidOutputRate{}\%. The failures therefore arose mainly from selecting the competing code, not from ignoring the requested format.
paper/main.tex:196:The findings concern one small quantized model and may not transfer to larger models or other quantization levels. Synthetic clause lookup is not natural contract analysis, and retrieval accuracy is not a measure of general capability. The \cpuBudgetMinutes{}-minute CPU budget capped the grid, leaving only \tierEightCount{} full-context probes at the longest tier and wide intervals throughout. That sparse tier prevents a conclusion about degradation within the measured range, and the experiment cannot address longer prompts. Greedy decoding removes run-to-run sampling variation but does not show how sampling would change the estimates. The mitigation is a deliberately simple keyword filter rather than a learned retrieval system.
